WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.049 --> 00:00:06.740
okay, here is some nice logical, just sensible
news, which is the democratic presidential

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:07.740
candidate.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:12.580
Andrew Yang has ruled out the possibility
of running third party or running independent

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:14.940
if he doesn't win the 2020 democratic nomination.

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:16.530
Now, why is this news?

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:22.109
It's news because if the goal is to defeat
Donald Trump, why would you do anything that

00:00:22.109 --> 00:00:24.109
makes a Donald Trump victory?

00:00:24.109 --> 00:00:30.880
More likely, which a third party run by a
former democratic, a presidential contender

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:35.690
would do, and this was literally his explanation
yesterday at the Washington post event.

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:41.260
He said, quote, I would never do anything
that would increase the chance of Donald Trump

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:43.219
becoming president again.

00:00:43.219 --> 00:00:47.210
The goal is to beat that man, get him out
of the oval office.

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:51.250
Now again, you might still be saying, but
David, why is this news?

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:53.630
Why is this something that you're talking
about?

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:58.210
It's news because there is a contingent of
the electorate in the United States, including

00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:04.340
on the left and it's a toxic contingent that
has a sort of burn it all down mentality.

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:10.270
If it's not my candidate, then I don't care
who wins, even if it's the worst person, and

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:13.470
I would even encourage, this is not me saying
it, it's them.

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:16.390
I would even encourage them to run third party.

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:21.530
I don't care if that takes just enough votes
from the eventual democratic nominee to allow

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:27.950
Donald Trump to slide into a second term,
and this is particularly relevant today because

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:32.790
it's the type of attitude that had people
on the left who didn't like Trump but also

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:39.810
didn't like Hillary staying home in 2016 because
so they said they're effectively the same

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:45.970
voting third party in 2016 and now Donald
Trump increasingly controls the judiciary

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:50.710
for decades with the Supreme court picks and
now more than 25% of high level judges have

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.560
been selected by Donald Trump.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:58.680
It ruins, he has ruined endless important
alliances, geopolitical alliances.

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:03.390
He has embarrassed the world in a way that
will take a very long time to recover from.

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:08.490
And that is why, this is great to just hear
from Andrew Yang and maybe this is actually

00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:11.800
a good time to talk a little more generally
about Andrew Yang.

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:18.140
Uh, most people in my audience know that I
was, uh, both one of the earliest people interviewing

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:23.020
Andrew Yang, I mean more well over a year
ago before he was getting very much attention.

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:26.700
I won't say I was the first person interviewing
him, but very early I got interested in talking

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:31.000
to Andrew Yang because we've been talking
about universal basic income for years at

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.740
this point on the show.

00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:36.460
But also my audience knows that I've been
critical of Andrew Yang when he has an idea

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:39.350
that I think is not 100% there, for example.

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:44.150
I also don't think that he's going to win
the nomination, but I don't really get some

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:47.330
of the attacks against Andrew Yang that I've
been seeing.

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:51.730
The idea of Andrew Yang is some kind of libertarian
Trojan horse.

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:53.680
It's very boring to me.

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:58.319
He appeals to some people who are on the center,
right?

00:02:58.319 --> 00:03:01.980
Tulsi Gabbert appeals to a bunch of people
that are on the right.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:05.950
The right, it would be wrong to say Tulsi
is a white supremacist because David Duke

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:07.670
endorsed her in the same way.

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:12.459
Yang is not, you know, some stealth right-wing
libertarian because some libertarians like

00:03:12.459 --> 00:03:13.459
him.

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:18.510
There is a fair criticism to make about Andrew
Yang that he sees politics sort of as like

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:23.750
a project management thing or, or like a consultancy
you bring in a business consultant than they

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:25.290
just figure out what tweaks to make.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:26.290
Okay.

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:27.290
That's a fair criticism.

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:33.410
Uh, you can say that Andrew Yang, uh, has
not fleshed out in detail the numbers behind

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:34.580
some of his proposals.

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:37.520
I was talking to a couple of people the other
day who have gone through the proposals in

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:38.520
detail.

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:44.040
They say the idea may still be a good idea,
but the numbers Andrew Yang has on his website

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:48.290
attached to some of these proposals and maybe
we'll do this in detail, not, I'm kind of

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:49.290
riffing here.

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:51.050
I wasn't prepared to do this in detail.

00:03:51.050 --> 00:03:53.850
Some of the numbers don't really add up, or
at least they're not complete enough.

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:55.810
He hasn't demonstrated that they work.

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:58.170
Those are all perfectly fair critiques.

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:04.790
I've been critical of the VAT tax proposal
of Andrew Yang, but Andrew Yang is clearly

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:07.340
not running to screw over Democrats.

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:12.180
He's clearly not running some kind of stealth
right-wing campaign and he's made it abundantly

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:16.599
clear that he's not going to do anything that
will help Donald Trump get reelected like

00:04:16.599 --> 00:04:17.959
running third party.

00:04:17.959 --> 00:04:23.879
Andrew Yang doesn't take cheap shots at other
candidates when he disagrees, he does it respectfully.

00:04:23.879 --> 00:04:29.069
He's pushed some important issues into the
conversation about taxation or large Corp

00:04:29.069 --> 00:04:31.129
taxation of large corporations.

00:04:31.129 --> 00:04:36.699
UBI automation, even if you don't think those
are the most important issues overall, we're

00:04:36.699 --> 00:04:39.409
better off with those issues as part of the
discussion.

00:04:39.409 --> 00:04:45.620
So in the same way that I said last week when
I talked about let's not idolize politicians,

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:52.330
uh, when you look w when, if you look at countries
where leaders are idolized and almost deified,

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:55.509
those are not countries that I think we want
to be like.

00:04:55.509 --> 00:04:58.309
Let's also not see everything in black and
white.

00:04:58.309 --> 00:05:04.310
Every candidate is either great or terrible,
good or evil, an honest actor or someone exhibiting

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:09.050
or, or, or you know, involved in some kind
of subterfuge to completely trick the electorate

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:10.650
about what they really are.

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:12.520
Andrew Yang has some interesting ideas.

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:14.680
You can be critical of his general approach.

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:19.189
He's being upfront, he's being, as far as
I see, honest about his intentions and his

00:05:19.189 --> 00:05:20.189
goals.

00:05:20.189 --> 00:05:22.599
And I think it's a great thing that he said,
no, I'm not going to do anything that will

00:05:22.599 --> 00:05:26.169
help Donald Trump win, uh, including, uh,
a third party run.

00:05:26.169 --> 00:05:27.669
If you disagree with me, let me know.

00:05:27.669 --> 00:05:33.680
I'm glad to hear reasonable arguments, um,
against Andrew Yang being a good faith actor.

00:05:33.680 --> 00:07:11.270
If you can put them together.

